Article 9 (Preparation of Fixed-Date Register)
(1) A fixed-date granting agency shall prepare a fixed-date register (hereinafter referred to as an "electronic fixed-date register") using a computerized information processing organization and record the following fixed-date information:
1. Fixed-date number;
2. Date of granting the fixed date;
3. Personal information of the lessor and lessee:
(a) For a natural person: Name, resident registration number (alien registration number for a foreigner), and address;
(b) For a corporation or organization other than a corporation: Corporate or organization name, corporate registration number or real-estate registration number, and location of principal office or main office;
4. Location of the housing;
5. Object of the lease;
6. Lease period;
7. Rent and deposit;
8. Name and date of birth of the applicant.
(2) Fixed-date information under paragraph (1) shall be preserved for 20 years.
(3) Information under paragraph (1) whose preservation period has expired shall, with authorization from the Minister of National Court Administration, be deleted by the end of March of the year following the year in which the preservation period expires.
